            <ArticleTitle>[Correlation analysis of the organometric heart parameters under normal and pathological conditions].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>24-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An organometric study of 27 heart parameters normally, in hypertension, chronic nonspecific pulmonary diseases and ischemic heart disease was carried out. Significant differences in the heart weight values under normal and pathological conditions were found. A correlation analysis of the heart parameters normally and pathologically was performed revealing specific associations for each group of pathology. Increased associations were observed between heart weight values and its parts and the linear-planimetric parameters in the groups of ischemic heart disease and chronic nonspecific pulmonary diseases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
